    "diagnosis": "Subependymal giant cell astrocytoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Axial T2-weighted MRI. A large lobulated mass that is T2-isointense to grey matter, arising from the foramen of Monro and causing mild hydrocephalus. Note is also made of the tiny T2-hypointense calcified subependymal nodules along the lining of the right lateral ventricle. There are also T2-hyperintensities in bilateral cerebral hemispheres, representing cortical/subcortical tubers. Overall features are characteristic of tuberous sclerosis.",
